      {
        "id": 5702,
        "name": "savagegreywolf",
        "username": "savagegreywolf",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/3ec8ea/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-05-01T00:31:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Another argument with my brother regarding the wording of cards. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/stuck_out_tongue.png?v=9\" title=\":stuck_out_tongue:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":stuck_out_tongue:\"> In Spite’s deck, the Potential Sidekick card reads: “At the start of each hero turn, that player may discard 3 cards. If they do, put this card under the Safe House card. At the start of the villain turn, each player draws 2 cards.”</p>\n<p>My reading of this is that if the potential sidekick is saved, everyone draws two cards. My brother read it that as long as the Potential Sidekick card is out, each player draws two cards.</p>\n<p>Anyone know how this one works?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:25.788Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 4,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 20.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5701,
        "topic_slug": "potential-sidekick",
        "display_username": "savagegreywolf",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
        "can_delete": false,
        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "Another argument with my brother regarding the wording of cards. :P In Spite's deck, the Potential Sidekick card reads: \"At the start of each hero turn, that player may discard 3 cards. If they do, put this card under the Safe House card. At the start of the villain turn, each player draws 2 cards.\"\n\nMy reading of this is that if the potential sidekick is saved, everyone draws two cards. My brother read it that as long as the Potential Sidekick card is out, each player draws two cards.\n\nAnyone know how this one works?",
        "actions_summary": [
